      "body": "## Overview\n\nPass size-only metadata to the encoder's existing sizing routine so supported dependency versions retain their exact rounding behavior without allocating pixels.\n\nDraft/WIP: focused regressions have been validated; human review and the remaining checks below are pending before this is ready.\n\n## Claims\n\nPass size-only metadata to the encoder's existing sizing routine so supported dependency versions retain their exact rounding behavior without allocating pixels.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated on a remote Ubuntu x86_64 machine with Ryzen 9 9900X, Python 3.12.13 and PyTorch 2.13.0+cpu, against base `698e79f3bdbbe4fe7d6be6d91b358a7f430753ab`.\n\n```sh\nTRITON_DEFAULT_BACKEND=cpu VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 PYTHONPATH=. ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/transformers_utils/processors/test_pixtral.py --confcutdir=tests/transformers_utils/processors -q\n```\n\nBaseline: 1 failed, 15 passed. Patched: 16 passed against both mistral-common 1.11.6 and 1.12.0.\n\nApplicable pre-commit checks passed. Upstream CI has not yet been evaluated for this draft.\n\n## Details\n\nFull model inference was not run; tests compare sizing with the existing dependency routine and check that pixel allocation is avoided.\n\nAI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used for analysis, implementation and validation. The submitter's human review remains pending.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Scoped to the reported contract and reuses existing behavior where possible.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Focused tests passed; remaining validation and human review are described above.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Applicable pre-commit checks passed.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Scope, evidence and limitations are recorded.\n</details>\n",
